IMPORT prelude

-- High Court (Admiralty Jurisdiction) Act 1961 (Singapore) -- which claims are admiralty claims (s 3(1)), when an action in rem
-- (arrest) lies against the ship, a sister ship or an aircraft (s 4(2)-(6), (8)), the limits on actions in personam for collisions
-- (s 5), wages claims on foreign ships (s 6), the Rhine Convention exclusion (s 7) and the Government saving (s 8(2)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/HCAJA1961.txt. The edition
-- says it incorporates amendments up to 1 December 2021; the latest amendment annotated in the text is Act 25 of 2021 wef
-- 01/04/2022 (s 5(2), (3)).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 5 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the jurisdictional decisions a
-- shipping practitioner meets: is the claim an admiralty claim, can the ship (or a sister ship, or an aircraft) be arrested, and can
-- a collision claim be brought in personam. Not encoded: s 3(2) (co-owners' accounts and sale), s 3(3) and (3A) (the content of
-- salvage claims), s 3(5), s 4(7) (title to sale proceeds), s 5(6) (Rules of Court), s 8(1) (receiver of wreck), the s 3(1)(i)
-- carve-out to section 168 of the Merchant Shipping Act 1995 (District Court salvage), and every cross-referenced Act.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `High Court (Admiralty Jurisdiction) Act 1961 -- arrest and jurisdiction`

§§ `3(1) -- the heads of admiralty jurisdiction`

-- s 3(1): "jurisdiction to hear and determine any of the following questions or claims": (a) possession or ownership of a ship;
-- (b) questions between co-owners "as to possession, employment or earnings"; (c) "a mortgage of or charge on a ship"; (d) "damage
-- done by a ship"; (e) "damage received by a ship"; (f) loss of life or personal injury from a defect in a ship or a wrongful act in
-- its navigation or management; (g) "loss of or damage to goods carried in a ship"; (h) agreements for carriage of goods or "the use
-- or hire of a ship"; (i) salvage; (j) towage; (k) pilotage; (l) "goods or materials supplied to a ship for her operation or
-- maintenance"; (m) "construction, repair or equipment of a ship or dock charges or dues"; (n) master's or crew's wages; (o)
-- disbursements; (p) general average; (q) bottomry; (r) forfeiture or condemnation, restoration after seizure, droits of admiralty.
-- s 3(4): applies to all ships "whether of Singapore or not and whether registered or not", to all claims "wheresoever arising",
-- and to mortgages "whether registered or not and whether legal or equitable, including mortgages and charges created under foreign
-- law". The rules below therefore take no account of flag, registration or place.
DECLARE Claim IS ONE OF
    `a claim to ownership of a ship`
    `a dispute between co-owners over earnings`
    `a claim under a ship mortgage`
    `a claim for damage done by a ship`
    `a claim for damage received by a ship`
    `a personal injury claim from a ship's negligent navigation`
    `a cargo damage claim`
    `a charterparty claim`
    `a salvage claim`
    `a towage claim`
    `a pilotage claim`
    `a bunker supplier's claim`
    `a ship repairer's claim`
    `a crew claim`
    `a master's disbursements claim`
    `a general average claim`
    `a bottomry claim`
    `a forfeiture claim`
    `a claim for unpaid rent on a shore office`

GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claim is within admiralty jurisdiction` IF
    CONSIDER `the claim`
    WHEN `a claim for unpaid rent on a shore office` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `4(2) and 4(4) -- which heads carry an action in rem`

-- s 4(2): in rem "against the ship or property in question" in the cases in s 3(1)(a), (b), (c) and (r).
GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claim is a proprietary head under section 4(2)` IF
    CONSIDER `the claim`
    WHEN `a claim to ownership of a ship` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a dispute between co-owners over earnings` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a claim under a ship mortgage` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a forfeiture claim` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 4(4): "In the case of any such claim as is mentioned in section 3(1)(d) to (q)".
GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claim is a section 3(1)(d) to (q) claim` IF
        `the claim is within admiralty jurisdiction` `the claim`
    AND (NOT `the claim is a proprietary head under section 4(2)` `the claim`)

GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claim is a crew claim` IF
    CONSIDER `the claim`
    WHEN `a crew claim` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `4(3)-(6), (8), 7 and 8(2) -- arresting the ship`

DECLARE `Arrest facts` HAS
    `the claim` IS A Claim
    `there is a maritime lien or other charge on the ship for the amount claimed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claim arises in connection with a ship` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the relevant person was owner, charterer, or in possession or control of the ship when the cause of action arose` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the relevant person now beneficially owns all the shares in the ship` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the relevant person is now the demise charterer of the ship` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the relevant person now beneficially owns all the shares in another ship` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the relevant person is now the demise charterer of another ship` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claim relates wholly or partly to wages` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the ship is a Government ship` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claim is against the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister has certified the claim as a Rhine Convention claim` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the ship is foreign and unregistered` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 7(1): no jurisdiction over a claim "certified by the Minister" to fall under the Rhine Navigation Convention; (2) proceedings
-- "shall be set aside".
-- s 8(2): nothing in the Act authorises "proceedings in rem in respect of any claim against the Government, or the arrest, detention
-- or sale of (a) any ship of which the beneficial interest is vested in the Government, or which is for the time being demised or
-- subdemised to or in the exclusive possession of the Government".
-- s 4(6): "Notwithstanding anything in subsections (1) to (5)", no action in rem on a s 3(1)(n) claim "unless the claim relates
-- wholly or partly to wages".
GIVEN f IS AN `Arrest facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `no bar to proceeding in rem` IF
        (NOT f's `the Minister has certified the claim as a Rhine Convention claim`)
    AND (NOT f's `the ship is a Government ship`)
    AND (NOT f's `the claim is against the Government`)
    AND `the claim is within admiralty jurisdiction` (f's `the claim`)
    AND (    (NOT `the claim is a crew claim` (f's `the claim`))
         OR  f's `the claim relates wholly or partly to wages`)

-- s 4(4)(a), (b): the claim "arises in connection with a ship" and the relevant person "was, when the cause of action arose, the
-- owner or charterer of, or in possession or in control of, the ship". s 4(8): in deciding whether a person "would be liable on a
-- claim in an action in personam, it shall be assumed that he has his habitual residence or a place of business within Singapore"
-- -- so the defendant's foreignness is not a fact this rule asks about.
GIVEN f IS AN `Arrest facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 4(4) gateway is met` IF
        `the claim is a section 3(1)(d) to (q) claim` (f's `the claim`)
    AND f's `the claim arises in connection with a ship`
    AND f's `the relevant person was owner, charterer, or in possession or control of the ship when the cause of action arose`

-- s 4(2): proprietary heads, in rem against the ship in question.
-- s 4(3): "In any case in which there is a maritime lien or other charge on any ship ... for the amount claimed", in rem against it.
-- s 4(4)(c): against "that ship, if at the time when the action is brought the relevant person is either the beneficial owner of that
-- ship as respects all the shares in it or the charterer of that ship under a charter by demise" -- "whether or not the claim gives
-- rise to a maritime lien".
GIVEN f IS AN `Arrest facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an action in rem lies against the ship` IF
        `no bar to proceeding in rem` f
    AND (    `the claim is a proprietary head under section 4(2)` (f's `the claim`)
         OR  f's `there is a maritime lien or other charge on the ship for the amount claimed`
         OR  (    `the section 4(4) gateway is met` f
              AND (    f's `the relevant person now beneficially owns all the shares in the ship`
                   OR  f's `the relevant person is now the demise charterer of the ship`)))

-- s 4(4)(d): against "any other ship of which, at the time when the action is brought, the relevant person is the beneficial owner
-- as respects all the shares in it". A demise charter is enough for the ship itself under (c), but not for another ship under (d).
GIVEN f IS AN `Arrest facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an action in rem lies against another ship` IF
        `no bar to proceeding in rem` f
    AND `the section 4(4) gateway is met` f
    AND f's `the relevant person now beneficially owns all the shares in another ship`

§§ `4(5) and 8(2)(b) -- arresting an aircraft`

-- s 4(5): towage or pilotage "in respect of an aircraft" -- in rem against that aircraft "if at the time when the action is brought
-- it is beneficially owned by the person who would be liable on the claim in an action in personam". s 8(2)(b): not "any aircraft
-- belonging to the Government". s 2: towage and pilotage of an aircraft mean "while the aircraft is waterborne".
GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim, `the aircraft is beneficially owned by the person liable` IS A BOOLEAN, `the aircraft belongs to the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an action in rem lies against the aircraft` IF
        `the aircraft is beneficially owned by the person liable`
    AND (NOT `the aircraft belongs to the Government`)
    AND (CONSIDER `the claim`
         WHEN `a towage claim` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a pilotage claim` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE)

§§ `5 -- collision claims in personam`

-- s 5(7): the section applies to "claims for damage, loss of life or personal injury arising out of a collision between ships or out
-- of the carrying out of or omission to carry out a manoeuvre ... or out of non-compliance ... with the collision regulations".
-- s 5(1): no action in personam unless (a) the defendant "has his habitual residence or a place of business within Singapore"; (b)
-- the cause of action arose "within inland waters of Singapore or within the limits of the port of Singapore"; or (c) an action "arising
-- out of the same incident or series of incidents" is proceeding or has been determined in the General Division.
-- s 5(2): not "until any proceedings previously brought by the claimant in any court outside Singapore against the same defendant in
-- respect of the same incident ... have been discontinued or otherwise come to an end".
-- s 5(3): (1) and (2) apply to counterclaims "(not being counterclaims in proceedings arising out of the same incident or series of
-- incidents)".
-- s 5(4): (1) to (3) do not apply "if the defendant thereto submits or has agreed to submit to the jurisdiction".
-- s 4(1): otherwise the jurisdiction "may in all cases be invoked by an action in personam".
DECLARE `Personam facts` HAS
    `the claim arises from a collision, manoeuvre or breach of the collision regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a counterclaim arising out of the same incident` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the defendant submits or has agreed to submit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the defendant has habitual residence or a place of business in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the cause of action arose in inland waters or port limits of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an action on the same incident is proceeding or determined in the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant's earlier foreign proceedings on the same incident are still on foot` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN p IS A `Personam facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a section 5(1) connecting factor is present` IF
        p's `the defendant has habitual residence or a place of business in Singapore`
    OR  p's `the cause of action arose in inland waters or port limits of Singapore`
    OR  p's `an action on the same incident is proceeding or determined in the General Division`

GIVEN p IS A `Personam facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may entertain the action in personam` IF
        (NOT p's `the claim arises from a collision, manoeuvre or breach of the collision regulations`)
    OR  p's `it is a counterclaim arising out of the same incident`
    OR  p's `the defendant submits or has agreed to submit`
    OR  (    `a section 5(1) connecting factor is present` p
         AND (NOT p's `the claimant's earlier foreign proceedings on the same incident are still on foot`))

§§ `6 -- wages on foreign ships`

-- s 6: "Nothing in this Act shall be construed as limiting the jurisdiction ... to refuse to entertain an action for wages by the master
-- or a member of the crew of a ship, not being a Singapore ship." The Act preserves the discretion only for non-Singapore ships; it
-- says nothing about Singapore ships (that no discretion exists for them is an inference not drawn here -- the rule says only where the
-- saving operates).
GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim, `the ship is a Singapore ship` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 6 preserves a discretion to refuse` IF
        `the claim is a crew claim` `the claim`
    AND (NOT `the ship is a Singapore ship`)
